Usage: skill-manager [-hvV] [--agent-context] [COMMAND]
Build tool for agent skills: CLI deps, skill references, MCP servers.
      --agent-context   Emit a bounded agent-facing context block to stderr
                          after the command.
  -h, --help            Show this help message and exit.
  -v, --verbose         Verbose output
  -V, --version         Print version information and exit.
Commands:
  list, ls        List installed units.
  artifacts       Name and inspect the artifacts this home derived.
  build           Rebuild derived artifacts — one, some, or everything stale.
  lock            Inspect units.lock.toml.
  install         Install a unit and its declared dependencies.
  uninstall, un   Uninstall a unit and clean up its side effects.
  remove, rm      Remove an installed unit (skill or plugin) from the store.
                    Lower-level than `uninstall` — by default does not unlink
                    agent symlinks or unregister MCP servers. Use `uninstall`
                    for the full cleanup.
  sync            Refresh installed units and re-run install side effects.
  upgrade         Upgrade installed git-tracked units — skills and plugins — to
                    the latest registry version (and optionally skill-manager
                    itself). Plugins re-register with Claude/Codex via their
                    CLIs after the bytes update so hooks reload.
  show            Show details for an installed unit.
  deps            Show the transitive dependency tree of an installed unit
                    (skill or plugin). For plugins, the tree includes both
                    plugin-level deps and every contained skill's deps (unioned
                    at parse time). With --who-imports, walk the edges
                    BACKWARDS instead: what in this home depends on the named
                    unit, across both `skill-imports` (addressed by name) and
                    manifest references (addressed by coordinate), transitively
                    and without looping.
  gateway         Manage the virtual MCP gateway process: up, down, attach,
                    detach, status.
  registry        Inspect or configure the skill registry.
  publish         Register a unit with the registry.
  search          Search the registry for skills and plugins (the KIND column
                    shows which). Sponsored slots are rendered separately and
                    can be hidden with --no-ads.
  policy          Inspect or initialize the skill-manager policy.
  pm              Manage bundled, version-pinned package managers (uv,
                    node/npm).
  cli             Inspect the CLI lock (which tools are installed, which skills
                    requested them).
  env             Materialize and run project-local uv environments.
  exec            Run a command bound to a Skill Manager home: export the
                    home's env, put its bin/ first on PATH, and refuse a launch
                    that would still read the global agent config. Use `--`
                    before a command with its own options.
  create          Scaffold a new skill or plugin directory.
  ads             Manage sponsored-placement campaigns on the registry.
  login           Authenticate against the registry and cache the bearer token.
  create-account  Register a new user on the registry.
  reset-password  Request a password-reset email for an account.
  onboard         Install the bundled skills (one shared install program) and
                    start the gateway.
  bind            Bind an installed unit or doc source to a target root.
  unbind          Reverse every projection from a binding and remove it from
                    the ledger.
  rebind          Move a binding to a new target root (unbind + bind in one
                    journal).
  bindings        Inspect the projection ledger (list | show <bindingId>).
  harness         Manage harness templates and their instances.
  home            Inspect, copy, describe, and set the policy of Skill Manager
                    homes.
  project         Register and inspect skill project manifests.
  sandbox         Inspect this process's sandbox.
  unit            Work with an installed unit as source: publish home edits
                    back to its repo.
